{
  "_comment": [
    "The bestiary. Twenty archetypes, each a stat block plus a body description.",
    "",
    "The timings are the difficulty, not the numbers: alertDelay is the tell before",
    "an enemy commits, circleTime is how long it spaces before attacking again, and",
    "recoverTime is the punish window you get afterwards. An enemy with a short",
    "recovery is not harder, it is unfair.",
    "",
    "body.kind is HUMANOID (arms, carries a weapon), CREATURE (a limb plan) or",
    "IMPORTED (an external model with its own animations, falling back to a",
    "procedural body when absent).",
    "",
    "drops rolls each row independently, so a kill can yield nothing, one thing",
    "or the whole table. Item ids come from items.json."
  ],

